Looking at line 910-924 in NCPInstanceBase-Addresses.cpp:
```cpp
if (entry.is_on_mesh() && entry.is_slaac() && prefix.get_length() == kSLAACPrefixLength
    && !has_slaac_on_mesh_prefix(prefix)
) {
    std::map<struct in6_addr, UnicastAddressEntry>::iterator addr_iter;
    addr_iter = find_address_with_prefix(prefix, kOriginThreadNCP);
    if (addr_iter != mUnicastAddresses.end()) {
        const struct in6_addr &address = addr_iter->first;
        ...
        unicast_address_was_removed(kOriginThreadNCP, address);
    }
}
```

The issue is: `unicast_address_was_removed` at line 610 erases the entry from `mUnicastAddresses` (line 620), then calls `mPrimaryInterface->remove_address(&address, entry.get_prefix_len())` at line 623.

But `mPrimaryInterface->remove_address` (in TunnelIPv6Interface.cpp line 447) also erases from `mUnicastAddresses` (line 453-455). However, the address was already erased from `mUnicastAddresses` in `NCPInstanceBase`, so the `TunnelIPv6Interface::remove_address` won't find it in its own `mUnicastAddresses` map.

